"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[4106],{24106:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"schemaVersion":1,"locale":"en","slug":"06-podushka","title":"Lesson 06. The cushion: How much, where and how to build it from zero","sourceFingerprint":"55fde8f1761a7584c3602edb66345570724830e9c922944a0e40fdb1ac988b11","blocks":[{"id":"b001","markdown":"## The cushion"},{"id":"b002","markdown":"How much, where and how to build it from zero"},{"id":"b003","markdown":"A financial cushion is a backup of your life. While a phone works, backing up photographs seems like unnecessary effort. You remember it when the phone is stolen or falls in water. With a backup, you lose an evening restoring it. Without one, you lose everything."},{"id":"b004","markdown":"A broken car, redundancy or urgent dental treatment: without a cushion, each becomes card debt at 50%. With a cushion, it is an expense after which you calmly rebuild the reserve. The cushion is not intended to make you rich. Its job is preventing the need to borrow."},{"id":"b005","markdown":"### How much you need"},{"id":"b006","markdown":"A typical guide is 3 to 6 months of essential expenses. Essential means basket 1 from lesson 2: housing, food, transport, communications, loan payments and medicine. If work goes wrong, restaurants and travel can pause; rent and food cannot."},{"id":"b007","markdown":"3–6 months roughly matches the time most people need to find work or recover after a serious setback. 3 months usually suffices when a family has 2 stable incomes, jobs are easy to find in your field, and there is no mortgage or dependants."},{"id":"b008","markdown":"6 months or more is needed for irregular income: freelancing, self-employment, business or heavy reliance on bonuses. Also if you are the sole breadwinner, have a mortgage or children, or work in a narrow field where job searches take time. Example: essential expenses of 70 000 RUB monthly mean a 3-month cushion of 210 000 RUB or a 6-month cushion of 420 000 RUB."},{"id":"b009","markdown":"Lesson 1 cited Russian Field: among Russians with savings, median runway was around 3.5 months. Even a minimal cushion puts you in the better half."},{"id":"b010","markdown":"### How to start from zero"},{"id":"b011","markdown":"A total of 200–400 thousand can seem intimidating, so build in stages. Each stage already makes you more resilient."},{"id":"b012","markdown":"- 1 month of essential expenses. This was lesson 5’s stage. If expensive debts exist, switch to repaying them after this."},{"id":"b013","markdown":"- 3 months once expensive debt is gone. Basic protection against losing work."},{"id":"b014","markdown":"- 6 months, especially if you belong to the risk groups above."},{"id":"b015","markdown":"The cushion can draw from 3 sources. First, the savings share and automatic transfer from lesson 3. Second, one-off money: bonuses, lesson 10’s tax refunds, gifts or selling unwanted belongings. Third, former leaks. A convenient rule for windfalls is “half to the cushion, half to yourself”."},{"id":"b016","markdown":"How large should the cushion be, and where should it stay?"},{"id":"b017","markdown":"Essential monthly expenses, basket 1: 70 000 RUB. Your circumstances:"},{"id":"b018","markdown":"Irregular income. Sole breadwinner. Mortgage or children. Narrow specialty. Target: 210 000 RUB."},{"id":"b019","markdown":"3 months of essential expenses."},{"id":"b020","markdown":"Stage 1: one month, 70 000 RUB. Stage 2: 3 months, 210 000 RUB. Savings account, about a month: 70 000 RUB. Partial-withdrawal deposit: 140 000 RUB. 3 months can suffice with 2 stable family incomes and easily found work. Keep the two parts in different banks."},{"id":"b021","markdown":"### Where to hold it"},{"id":"b022","markdown":"The cushion has 3 requirements, and return is not foremost. Access within 1–2 days, no exposure to market losses, and interest to keep inflation from consuming it. Split it into 2 parts, like a wallet and a savings box: the wallet is always accessible, the box is safer but slower to reach."},{"id":"b023","markdown":"#### First part: a savings account"},{"id":"b024","markdown":"Around one month’s expenses. Withdraw or add at any time without losing interest."},{"id":"b025","markdown":"Choose daily-balance interest. Some accounts calculate interest on the month’s minimum balance. Their advertised rate is often higher, but a mid-month withdrawal earns nothing on the withdrawn amount for the whole month. This portion may be withdrawn, so that arrangement does not suit it."},{"id":"b026","markdown":"The disadvantage is that the bank may change a savings-account rate on any day."},{"id":"b027","markdown":"#### Second part: a partial-withdrawal deposit"},{"id":"b028","markdown":"Everything else. The rate is fixed throughout the term, useful when rates fall as they currently are. Choose 3–6 months with partial withdrawal without forfeiting interest. Closing a conventional fixed-term deposit early can recalculate interest almost to zero."},{"id":"b029","markdown":"#### Not all in one place"},{"id":"b030","markdown":"You do not keep a spare house key on the main keyring: both could be lost together. Leave it with parents or neighbours. Likewise, hold the cushion’s parts in different banks plus some cash at home. If one bank blocks your card or its app stops working, the other parts remain available."},{"id":"b031","markdown":"THE CUSHION IN SEPARATE PLACES. BANK 1: SAVINGS ACCOUNT, ~1 MONTH. BANK 2: DEPOSIT FOR THE REST, PARTIAL WITHDRAWAL. CASH AT HOME FOR A WEEK OR TWO. THE SPARE KEY BELONGS ON A DIFFERENT RING."},{"id":"b032","markdown":"### Deposit insurance"},{"id":"b033","markdown":"Deposits and account balances at a member bank are state-insured through the Deposit Insurance Agency, or DIA. The limit is 1.4 million RUB per person per bank, including accrued interest. If a bank loses its licence, the agency repays within that limit."},{"id":"b034","markdown":"This comfortably covers most cushions. If the amount approaches the limit, divide it between 2 banks. Check membership on the DIA website."},{"id":"b035","markdown":"### Which currency"},{"id":"b036","markdown":"Keep a cushion in the currency you spend. If rent, food and dentistry are paid in rubles, the cushion should be in rubles."},{"id":"b037","markdown":"A backup must also restore quickly. A copy that takes a week to retrieve from the other side of the world on the day of a disaster is nearly useless. Foreign currency held “just in case” is similar. When money is urgently needed, it must first be sold, possibly at a poor rate. Currency diversification protects savings and belongs to the next module, rather than the emergency cushion."},{"id":"b038","markdown":"An exception is regular foreign-currency spending, such as a child’s overseas education. Part of the cushion can reasonably match it. A week or two of cash at home is that spare key, useful if cards and apps temporarily fail."},{"id":"b039","markdown":"### What does not count as a cushion"},{"id":"b040","markdown":"A credit limit: borrowed money at 50%. Shares, bonds and funds that may fall just when money is needed. Crypto for the same reasons, more strongly. A home or car that cannot sell quickly without loss. And “I will ask my parents”: that is hope rather than money."},{"id":"b041","markdown":"### When to use it"},{"id":"b042","markdown":"Use the cushion for situations simultaneously unexpected, urgent and necessary: job loss, treatment, urgent repair, or fixing a car required for work. A sale, new phone or last-minute holiday does not qualify; those have lesson 3’s goal accounts. If you draw from the cushion, replenish it first. Until restored, it is again the main priority."},{"id":"b043","markdown":"### Tax on interest"},{"id":"b044","markdown":"With substantial savings, understand the tax. Deposit and savings-account interest is subject to personal income tax only above a tax-free allowance. The allowance equals 1 million RUB multiplied by the highest key rate on the 1st day of each month of the year."},{"id":"b045","markdown":"On January 1, 2026, the rate was 16% and it had not gone higher during the year. Thus, for 2026, total interest of 160 000 RUB across all banks is tax-free. At rates around 13%, that corresponds to roughly 1.2 million RUB of savings; below that, the tax does not affect you."},{"id":"b046","markdown":"The tax authority calculates and sends a notice. Tax for 2026 is payable by December 1, 2027."},{"id":"b047","markdown":"### The essentials"},{"id":"b048","markdown":"- A cushion is 3–6 months of essential expenses. Its job is removing the need to borrow."},{"id":"b049","markdown":"- Build in stages: 1 month, then 3, then 6."},{"id":"b050","markdown":"- Hold it in daily-balance savings or partial-withdrawal deposits, in your spending currency."},{"id":"b051","markdown":"- The DIA insurance limit is 1.4 million RUB per bank."},{"id":"b052","markdown":"The cushion is built; now protect it. It is often lost through a single phone call rather than inflation or crisis. That is the next lesson."}],"terms":[{"id":"asv","term":"Deposit Insurance Agency (DIA)","definition":"The state mechanism paying a depositor up to 1.4 million RUB per bank if its licence is revoked or it fails. Holding more than this in one bank is therefore imprudent."},{"id":"inflyatsiya","term":"Inflation","definition":"A rise in the general price level. In practice: there is more money and the same quantity of goods, so each item costs more. You have not become richer; price tags have simply risen."},{"id":"klyuchevaya-stavka","term":"Key interest rate","definition":"The rate at which the central bank lends to banks. The main monetary-policy tool and the economy’s “price of money”. A higher rate makes loans more expensive and slows inflation."},{"id":"ndfl","term":"Personal income tax (NDFL)","definition":"Personal income tax. This course’s educational calculations use 13% up to 2.4 million RUB of annual income and 15% for the next band. Since 2025 the main scale has been progressive; special rules apply to other types of income. Check current rates and deduction eligibility with the Federal Tax Service."},{"id":"obligatsiya","term":"Bond","definition":"A debt security. You are a lender, not an equity owner: you lend at a fixed coupon and principal is returned at maturity. Risk is lower than for shares."},{"id":"strakhovanie-vkladov","term":"Deposit insurance","definition":"A state guarantee to repay depositors up to a certain amount if a bank fails. In Russia, 1.4 million RUB per bank through the Deposit Insurance Agency."},{"id":"dokhodnost","term":"Yield","definition":"The annual percentage an investment actually earns at today’s price. A bond’s price and yield move in opposite directions: falling price means rising yield. Government-bond yields influence loan and deposit rates."},{"id":"neoblagaemyy-limit","term":"Tax-free interest allowance","definition":"The amount of annual deposit interest exempt from personal income tax: 1 million RUB multiplied by the year’s maximum key rate. The tax authority calculates and notifies tax above the allowance; no separate filing is needed."}],"quizzes":[{"id":"06-podushka-q1","q":"Essential expenses are 60 000 RUB monthly, total spending 90 000 RUB. What is a minimum 3-month cushion?","options":["270 000 RUB","180 000 RUB","60 000 RUB"],"correct":1},{"id":"06-podushka-q2","q":"Why prefer daily-balance interest to minimum-balance interest for a cushion?","options":["The daily-balance rate is always higher","That account is tax-exempt","A mid-month withdrawal under minimum-balance rules loses interest on the withdrawn amount for the whole month"],"correct":2},{"id":"06-podushka-q3","q":"Which can count as an emergency cushion?","options":["Money in a savings account at an insured bank","A credit-card limit","Shares in a large company"],"correct":0}],"officialSources":[]}')}}]);